  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $y=-\\frac{7}{3}ln\u2061x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{7}{3}ln\u2061x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
